enge directly: - Were they lying? No. They were repeating a widely believed mistake. - Is there a still-something to the old idea? Yes — the liquid-like structure. But that something doesn’t make it a flowing liquid. It makes it an amorphous solid. And that distinction is the whole point. I’m not asking you to believe in a world of lying educators. I’m asking you to see that a structural curiosity got misinterpreted as a material property, and that misinterpretation became a very sticky story. The story had a kernel of truth, but it was applied to the wrong timescale.
