vetted documentary. You *should* be able to. But even the best science communication sometimes fails to catch up with corrections. The glass-flow story is a textbook example of a zombie fact—it's been killed by research, but it keeps shambling back onto screens and into classrooms because it's just so compelling. So your memory of that documentary is real, and your trust in it was well-placed at the time. You just happened to catch one of those rare moments where the "vetted" information was itself outdated. It happens. And now you know the rest of the story.
